{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-header",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": -360
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Sinnamary RF Pixel Classification — Phase 3",
        "params": {
          "text": "# Sinnamary RF Pixel Classification — Phase 3  (4-class, spatial split)\n\n**Goal:** Supervised pixel classification of the Sinnamary coast using a **Random Forest** trained on the 12-band S1+S2 fused stack with **ESA WorldCover 2021** as ground truth labels.\n\n## Pipeline\n🟦 **Feature engineering (S1+S2):** 12-band stack — 6 S1 polarisation features (RVI, Span, Span_dB, NRPB, PDI, DPSVI) + raw VV/VH/ratio + NDVI/MNDWI/EVI.\n🟩 **Ground truth:** ESA WorldCover 2021 (10 m → 20 m). Classes 90 (Herbaceous wetland) merged into 95 → unified **CoastalVeg** class.\n🟧 **Random Forest Classifier:** Spatial block split (50 px blocks ≈ 1 km), per-class sample caps, RF 100 trees.\n\n## 4-class model\n| Value | Class | Training signal |\n|-------|-------|-----------------|\n| **95** | CoastalVeg (Mangroves + Wetland) | merged 90+95, cap 15 000 |\n| **10** | Tree cover | inland forest, cap 8 000 |\n| **80** | Permanent water | river / estuary, cap 8 000 |\n| **60** | Bare/sparse (orpaillage) | cap 8 000 |\n\n## Spatial autocorrelation fix\nSpatial block split (50 px = 1 km at 20 m) avoids train/test pixel adjacency. OA is lower but honest.",
          "width": 2060,
          "height": 300,
          "fontSize": 13,
          "color_index": 4
        }
      },
      "width": 1105,
      "height": 447,
      "selected": false,
      "positionAbsolute": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": -360
      },
      "dragging": false
    },
